  "not_simulated": [
    {
      "what": "the body diode",
      "why": "Each BSS138 is the engine's nmos, which has no body diode. Pulling the high side low still pulls the low side low, because a negative drain-to-source voltage swaps the terminals and the gate is held at LV. The datasheet's diode, 0.8 V typical, is not a separate part."
    },
    {
      "what": "the drawing's marks",
      "why": "The Eagle board carries a logo, fiducials and silkscreen. This model is the 15.24 x 12.7 mm outline. The product page lists 16.05 x 13.33 mm overall, the board with the headers past that outline. The mask colour is not a maker's colour."
    },
    {
      "what": "bus capacitance beyond the parts",
      "why": "A rise is set by the 10 kohm pull-ups and the BSS138 capacitances. Wiring and a device's own pins add capacitance this module does not include."
    }
  ],
